WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:05.540
There are many shows we remember fondly from
our childhoods, from the adventures of the

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.620
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles to the Saturday
morning cartoons of The Flintstones or The

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:17.120
Jetsons, but arguably the most famous of these
cartoons is Spongebob Squarepants, a show

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.830
about an optimistic sea sponge and his daily
life throughout his city of Bikini Bottom.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.320
We all know the same Spongebob Squarepants
in some way or some form.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.610
His popularity translated to a lot of merchandise.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:37.170
From plushes to lunchboxes and phone cases,
Spongebob is a staple of childhood and modern-day

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.170
culture.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.330
While the SCP Foundation’s world is one
where monsters roam and anomalous events affect

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:49.239
millions, Spongebob, and his merchandise,
is also popular within this universe.

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:54.350
The SCP Foundation is most well known for
its protection of normalcy from the most extreme

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.370
and dangerous threats.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:04.750
Anomalies such as SCP-1730 the inter-dimensional
Site 13, SCP-001 When Day Breaks, or SCP-682

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.399
the humanity-hating, Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:13.310
These SCPs pose a direct, obvious threat to
the people of the SCP universe.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:18.090
A lot of these anomalies have object classes
that clearly state the danger level, along

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.779
with their level of containment difficulty:
Keter, Apollyon, Euclid and more.

00:01:23.779 --> 00:01:28.079
Safe class anomalies are not commonly thought
of as dangerous, but what about those safe

00:01:28.079 --> 00:01:34.189
class anomalies that were specifically made
to be inconspicuously dangerous to humankind?

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:37.700
Today we take a deep dive into one such anomaly.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.819
And we don’t mean scuba diving.

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:41.399
Or…do we?

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:49.819
Anyhow, here is a look at SCP-1808 also known
as the “Spongebob Watches”.

00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:54.420
Its containment procedures are almost too
simple, but given it’s a safe class anomaly,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.759
it’s all about the difficulty of putting
it in a box and keeping it in there more than

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:00.710
being about it’s danger level.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:07.229
There are six instances of SCP-1808, and all
are kept in standard, safe-class anomaly storage

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.069
lockers in Safe Wing-C at Site-25.

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:17.120
This is similar to the containment procedures
of SCP-662: The Butler’s Handbell, which

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.709
also is a relatively safe anomaly all things
considered.

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:25.310
The containment procedures also mention that
all testing outside of monitored environments

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.580
is expressly prohibited.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.921
It begs the question: if this safe-class anomaly
can be kept in simple storage lockers, why

00:02:32.921 --> 00:02:36.180
is there such a strict mandate against testing?

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.939
What potential danger could SCP-1808 pose
that these restrictions are placed on it?

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:47.079
Well, to properly answer all of your amazingly
inquisitive questions, we need to look back

00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:53.120
on the story of how SCP-1808 came into the
Foundation’s possession to begin with.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.499
In early April of 2004, the Foundation was
alerted to an ongoing anomalous item auction

00:02:58.499 --> 00:03:02.810
from the anomalous group of interest Mashall,
Carter, and Dark.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:07.489
Anomalous groups of interest within the SCP
Foundation’s universe are all but rare.

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:12.340
From the malicious Choas Insurgency that works
to harm the Foundation by utilizing anomalies

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:18.760
as weapons, to SCP-610 which uses Yaldaboth
worshipping Sarkic Cults that work to bring

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:24.150
humankind back to a primal way of living,
these groups are known for their use of the

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.639
anomalous for executing their plans - and
as we’ve seen time and time again on this

00:03:28.639 --> 00:03:32.030
channel - by pretty much any means they deem
necessary.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.799
Let’s just say there’s not many boundaries
set.

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:36.799
Or none.

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:40.239
Let’s go NO boundaries.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.239
moving on.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:44.920
When it comes to Marshall, Carter, and Dark,
however, they are a bit different from these

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.190
groups.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:51.030
Instead of calling upon the starfish god like
the Fifthists or rebuilding the god of technology

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:56.500
Mekhane like the Church of the Broken God,
Marshall, Carter, and Dark have one motive:

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.500
profit.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.610
This group is solely dedicated to selling
and profiting from the anomalous, whether

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.719
that be through selling to the highest 1%
of the 1% or contracting their anomalies out

00:04:06.719 --> 00:04:11.560
to other anomalous organizations for high
payments, Marshall, Carter, and Dark is in

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.079
the world of leveraging the anomalous for
money and as much money as possible.

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:21.139
The SCP Foundation normally has a somewhat
cordial relationship with Marshall, Carter,

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:25.650
and Dark, sometimes even purchasing anomalies
from the group for containment purposes.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:32.750
However, Marshall, Carter, and Dark often
overstep these boun- boundaries, causing the

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.350
SCP Foundation to have to intervene and “steal”
anomalies from them.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:43.110
The story of SCP-1808 is one of these times
the Foundation had to step in.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:48.300
An agent of Mobile Task Force Eta-2 ("Buyer
Beware"), Agent Rosser, was working covertly

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.560
within the ranks of Marshall, Carter, and
Dark, attaining information that may be needed

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.030
for the SCP Foundation’s containment efforts.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:05:00.780
Agent Rosser was of course under strict protocols
set forward by the SCP Foundation.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:05.420
He was to keep them updated with any movements
Marshall, Carter, and Dark may be making,

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:11.060
noting any potential anomalies that may need
containing, and always making sure to be checking-in

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.250
every day.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.949
On April 4th, Agent Rosser failed to do his
required check-in, and the Foundation immediately

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:21.990
deployed other “Buyer Beware” MTF Agents
to his last known location - a Marshall, Carter,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.840
and Dark auction house.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.229
The raid commenced, and the SCP Foundation,
having some of the most highly trained and

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:33.460
sophisticated soldiers and agents in the world,
swiftly took the upper hand, restraining and

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.660
apprehending members of Marshall, Carter,
and Dark and their potential buyers.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:42.740
A large-scale search then commenced for Agent
Rosser within the auction house, where he

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:48.759
was found seated behind a curtain with all
six instances of SCP-1808 attached to his

00:05:48.759 --> 00:05:54.229
body: one on each of his wrists and ankles,
and two fastened together around his neck.

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:58.610
Agent Rosser was found in a state that could
only be described as pure torment.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.680
He was unrecognizable.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:06.040
The bones of his fingers and his toes were
so elongated they circled back onto themselves.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:10.050
The skin of his hands and feet were torn to
shreds from the force of whatever was pulling

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.050
at them.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.740
The Foundation-issued boots Agent Rosser wore
were ripped as well to make way for the bones.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.800
And possibly the most ghastly of all, his
teeth had grown out of his mouth, tearing

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.199
the skin of his cheeks and jaw.

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:26.759
Could it be that these simple Spongebob watches
were the cause of this torture?

00:06:26.759 --> 00:06:31.050
There was no other obvious threat observed
that could possibly be the cause of these

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.869
changes to his body.

00:06:32.869 --> 00:06:35.800
This made the Foundation suspicious and worried.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:38.080
What else could be instore for them?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:44.050
The SCP-1808 file describes the anomaly as
a set of six, yellow plastic wristwatches.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:48.659
These watches are patterned with green dots
scattered around the watch body along with

00:06:48.659 --> 00:06:52.629
images of the famous cartoon character Spongebob
Squarepants.

00:06:52.629 --> 00:06:58.530
The first anomalous property of SCP-1808 is
that no matter what mechanical or electronic

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:03.790
parts are removed, the watch still operates
as if it’s perfectly intact.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:09.129
The most dangerous part of SCP-1808 is when
its placed on a person or animal.

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:15.169
As long as the wearer has limbs and phalanx
bones, SCP-1808’s main anomalous property

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:16.629
will affect them.

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:23.080
Once put on, SCP-1808 can not be removed unless
the person who put it on decides to take it

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.080
off.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:30.120
Once placed, those wearing SCP-1808 will hear
a chime of Spongebob’s famous, or infamous,

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.349
chuckle every 15 minutes.

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:37.680
If hearing that wasn’t suffering enough,
SCP-1808’s anomalous property will now begin

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.479
to affect the wearer.

00:07:39.479 --> 00:07:45.360
After this laugh is heard, the bones in whatever
hand the person is wearing SCP-1808 will begin

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.970
to grow in length.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:54.729
Every 15 minutes as long as SCP-1808 is worn,
these bones will extend about 6 cm until the

00:07:54.729 --> 00:07:55.979
watch is removed.

00:07:55.979 --> 00:08:00.550
The skin around the bones does not grow, so
once they get long enough, the bones will

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.419
tear through and rip the skin to continue
growing.

00:08:03.419 --> 00:08:09.139
While there is no blood loss once this happens,
those who have worn SCP-1808 describe the

00:08:09.139 --> 00:08:11.509
growing as immensely painful.

00:08:11.509 --> 00:08:15.370
These changes do not have to be permanent,
should the person that placed it on the poor

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:19.880
soul who has to suffer these consequences
feel a bit of mercy, they can retract the

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:23.740
adjustment knob of the watch and rotate it
counterclockwise.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:28.270
Upon doing this, the bones will begin to shrink
back to their original size, and the ripped

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:34.830
and torn skin will anomalously heal back to
its normal state as if SCP-1808 never affected

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:35.830
it.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.760
While the physical harm that SCP-1808 inflicts
on its victims can be reversed, the memory

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:45.670
of the pain and torment the victims went through
will be fully remembered, potentially causing

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.890
further psychological torment even when the
watches are removed.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:55.270
The item’s description also includes the
terrifying note that two instances of SCP-1808

00:08:55.270 --> 00:09:00.500
can be placed around a subjects neck, and
instead of lengthening any bones in the neck,

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:04.690
it will instead mercilessly cause the victim’s
teeth to grow.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.810
In the case of Agent Rosser, we now know the
suffering he was going through during his

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.300
time as a spy for the SCP Foundation.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.300
Yikes!

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:17.630
The potential danger these watches can pose
if in the wrong hands - no pun intended of

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.850
course - can be devastating.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:23.230
What if an authoritarian government purchased
these anomalies?

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:28.800
The torture SCP-1808 inflicts upon it’s
victims could easily be used to squeeze information

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.660
out of a person of interest.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:36.250
Same goes for the Choas Insurgency, who could
use these anomalies to attack the SCP Foundation

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:40.650
and gain classified information only someone
like a member of the Overseer Command would

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:41.690
know.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.070
These anomalies had to be contained.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:48.200
The Foundation quickly restrained the Marshall,
Carter, and Dark agent inflicting this horrible

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:53.160
torture on Agent Rosser and forced him to
return Agent Rosser’s deformaties back to

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.950
normal and hand over the watches.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.430
Questions circled in the Foundation’s minds.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:02.290
Why was there no blood despite the amount
of damage on Agent Rosser’s skin?

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:07.020
And why did the Marshall, Carter, and Dark
agents do this to him in the first place?

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:11.890
A Foundation Doctor conducted an interview
with Agent Rosser with hopes to figure it

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:12.890
all out.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:17.410
The doctor began with a simple statement:
“Kindly summarize the events leading up

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:18.690
to your abduction.”

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.940
Rosser answered: “There was nothing crazy
about my abduction.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:25.330
I went to sleep in my flat and woke up tied
to a table.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.480
Maybe I was drugged, but i’m not sure.”

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.980
This confused the doctor.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:33.610
Normally, when an undercover SCP Foundation
agent is discovered they are not treated with

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.580
the relative kindness Agent Rosser was shown.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:41.680
These groups, especially those such as Marshall,
Carter, and Dark, normally want information,

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:44.260
and will take that by any means necessary.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:48.650
The doctor continues with his questioning:
“How did Marshall, Carter &amp; Dark come to

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.770
discover your identity as a Foundation field
agent?”

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:55.730
Rosser chuckles: “I was never compromised
as an agent.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.840
You see, I don't think they were even aware
I was Foundation.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:02.350
If they were, they would have called off the
auction and gotten their goods the hell outta

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:03.350
there.”

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:06.980
He goes on to say that he didn’t even tell
his friends or family any details that would

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:10.290
have made them suspicious of his rank in the
Foundation.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:14.680
Once again, the doctor was extremely confused
by this move on Marshall, Carter, and Dark’s

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.680
part.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.690
If they didn’t know Agent Rosser was of
the SCP Foundation, why did they torture him?

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:26.600
The doctor asks this question to Agent Rosser:
“If your identity wasn't compromised, why

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.730
were you abducted and tortured?”

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.200
Agent Rosser responds “I think it was quality
assurance.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.560
Testing the product, making sure it worked.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:35.900
Experimenting with it.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:40.360
And if the raid hadn't happened, they would
have put me on stage and demonstrated it.”

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:44.450
Like the SCP Foundation, Marshall, Carter,
and Dark are more than willing to test out

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:47.090
these anomalies on unwilling subjects.

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:52.010
Perhaps they see their employees like the
SCP Foundation sees the D-Class personnel.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:56.770
At least the D-Class personnel are death row
inmates - they’re people who committed heinous

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:01.960
crimes, whereas Agent Rosser and his coworkers
were innocent people trying to make a living.

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:06.480
We see how brutal the world of a profit-driven
anomalous group could be with what happened

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:11.090
to Agent Rosser, and one could only imagine
the horrifying torment the former employees

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:16.150
of Marshall, Carter, and Dark may have went
through under this so-called “quality assurance.”

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.810
Agent Rosser continues with his story.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:22.290
He describes the events leading up to the
watches being placed on him.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.320
He drowsily awoke in a dark room strapped
to a table.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:28.520
He recognized the room he was in as the basement.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:32.530
He looked to his left and then his right when
his stomach dropped - he wasnt the only one

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:33.710
down there.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:38.700
Next to him were people he recognized as his
coworkers, strapped to tables like him.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.820
After this realization, his shock turned to
fear as senior members of Marshall, Carter,

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.490
and Dark entered the room.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.930
“We are downsizing” one of them said to
the helpless employees.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:53.860
They were going to use them as guinea pigs
for their twisted testing of their products.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:58.350
Agent Rosser gets distracted, describing how
much he used to enjoy the Spongebob Squarepants

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.750
television show.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:05.260
He watched it recently and found it funny,
but now, all he could think of is that laugh.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:10.940
Every fifteen minutes, that laugh signified
more torture, more torment that he had to

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.010
be put through.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:16.910
Now, he can’t imagine watching the show
without thinking of the torment SCP-1808 and

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.820
Marshall, Carter, and Dark put him through.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:24.760
While the physical scars are gone, the mental
ones still awfully remain.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:28.990
The doctor interviewing him requests that
Agent Rosser stays on the topic of SCP-1808.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:35.540
The agent apologizes and continues “First
they just strapped the watches to my wrists

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.640
and ankles and waited.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:41.630
After they were sure the things went off every
fifteen minutes, they started twisting the

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.710
little knobs,”
He describes that he knew he was definitely

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.110
being tested on.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:50.930
The Marshall, Carter, and Dark senior staff
were observing these tests the entire time,

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.730
and even participated.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.500
The experimenters would twist the knobs mercilessly
until the bones in his hands and feet tore

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:02.190
free of the skin and hit the walls of the
basement, only for them to crank them back

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:05.560
and begin the process over again.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:10.370
You can only imagine how many times they did
this to the agent, for no other purpose but

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.850
“quality assurance”.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:17.550
Agents of the SCP Foundation are trained to
withstand awful torture so that no confidential

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:21.980
or important information is revealed to other
groups of interest or the public.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:26.280
Agent Rosser, being trained by the Foundation,
would know this training.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:31.680
He attempted to use his training methods to
resist the torture but it, sadly, wasnt enough.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.790
Agent Rosser states “The pain was from the
inside.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:39.330
The tips of my fingers were worn off and peeled
back like an old pair of gloves.”

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:43.430
He was one of the lucky ones, though, the
people chained to the tables in the same room

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:47.570
he was in didn’t survive whatever twisted
torture they went through at the hands of

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.290
Marshall, Carter, and Dark.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:53.730
The doctor realizes that part of Agent Rosser’s
story is being over looked and states “When

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:57.830
you were discovered, two of the watches had
been joined together and fastened around your

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:58.830
neck.”

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.330
Agent Rosser is silent.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:04.600
This was clearly the most horrifying part
of this entire ordeal for him.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:08.980
His silence persists for another minute and
the doctor calls his name “Agent Rosser?”

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.980
Rosser shakily begins.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:15.300
Apparently the Marshall, Carter, and Dark
senior staff weren’t impressed with the

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:21.630
effects of SCP-1808, despite the clear signs
of pain and anguish from Agent Rosser.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:25.210
They thought it needed to be improved for
a higher sale price.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.510
One of them suggested placing two of the watches
around his throat.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:34.490
Rosser described how his teeth began to grow:
“My teeth started getting longer, like my

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.570
fingers and toes.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:40.070
But they didn't go straight, they went off
in different directions.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:42.160
Some went … inside.”

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:47.160
Rosser explains that all he could hear every
time his teeth grew was that infamous Spongebob

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.160
laugh.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:52.150
He goes on to tell the doctor that this torture
impressed the senior staff of Marshall, Carter,

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:55.070
and Dark enough to continue with a sale.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:59.580
The memory of this makes Agent Rosser ill,
and he vomits before he can even finish the

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:00.580
thought.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:03.120
The doctor allows Agent Rosser to be dismissed.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:07.310
Hopefully he was provided with some Class-A
Amnestics to forget this whole ordeal.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:13.190
The Foundation didn’t contain SCP-3000 and
harvest the Y-909 compound for nothing remember.

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:18.550
The SCP-1808 file also includes a recovered
auction catalogue that Marshall, Carter, and

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:23.310
Dark would have used to describe SCP-1808
to potential buyers.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:28.030
The description goes on to read: “These
watches are the only products in existence

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:33.300
with such uncanny abilities, and businesses
or individuals wishing to carry out quick,

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.840
efficient, and mess-free interrogations would
be remiss in missing this once-in-a-lifetime

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:42.590
opportunity to acquire them, as would our
patrons with tastes for intimate sessions

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.690
of impassioned discomfort.”

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:49.520
The starting bid on SCP-1808: only 14,600
pounds.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:55.020
Marshall, Carter, and Dark had no issue selling
these watches to those who wanted to inflict

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.760
awful torture on their unwilling and unknowing
victims.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.790
And we thought the SCP Foundation was willing
to stomp moral boundaries.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:08.409
All it took was a little motivation for profits,
and Marshall, Carter, and Dark were shamelessly

00:17:08.409 --> 00:17:09.929
off to the races.

00:17:09.929 --> 00:17:17.559
For a few rather normal looking Spongebob-themed
watches, SCP-1808 is truly a terrifying anomaly.

00:17:17.559 --> 00:17:22.240
Thanks to Agent Rosser’s sacrifice, they
are no longer on wrists and necks and are

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:26.350
now in - Shall we say - better hands with
the Foundation.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:30.379
In the case of Marshall, Carter and Dark,
they suspended their morality to the point

00:17:30.379 --> 00:17:32.909
of testing the anomaly on their own employees.

00:17:32.909 --> 00:17:38.220
I guess this goes to show that profits over
people is more than just a scary concept,

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.139
even in the world of the SCP Foundation.

00:17:41.139 --> 00:17:46.720
Now go check out “How Does the SCP Foundation
Actually Make Money” and “SCP-738 The

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:51.919
Devil’s Deal” for more on anomalous business
transactions that might just cost more than

00:17:51.919 --> 00:17:53.059
you can bargain for!

